{
    "word": "безо",
    "lang_code": "ru",
    "source_file_to_entries": {
        "raw-wiktextract-data.jsonl": [],
        "ru-extract.jsonl": [
            {
                "entry_id": "f6b8a515-4182-35c0-ba38-f367b527597f",
                "word": "безо",
                "pos": "prep",
                "lang_code": "ru",
                "forms": [],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "f57c91dc-c6c8-3a5c-b72f-17967408352c",
                        "entry_id": "f6b8a515-4182-35c0-ba38-f367b527597f",
                        "glosses": [
                            "то же, что без, употребляется перед родительным падежом местоимений весь и всякий и (вариативно с без) некоторых односложных существительных с беглыми гласными в корне (лёд, лоб, сон)"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "fa24f560-3679-4b36-a5a6-f9dc2d274d1a",
                                "sense_id": "f57c91dc-c6c8-3a5c-b72f-17967408352c",
                                "text": "Она появилась на вокзале, мы ехали с охраной, в пустом вагоне безо всяких удобств."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "46d987d5-f27b-4d43-b363-8531bb30770c",
                                "sense_id": "f57c91dc-c6c8-3a5c-b72f-17967408352c",
                                "text": "Контакты искрят ― и мы без любви, без ненависти, безо всех этих провинциальных драм отнюдь не испытываем недостатка в адреналине."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "c76ad52f-bfcc-4a68-88ed-05a2d1ad44d6",
                                "sense_id": "f57c91dc-c6c8-3a5c-b72f-17967408352c",
                                "text": "― Сделайте, пожалуйста, по моему совету, ― сказала старая княгиня, ― сверху положите бумажку и ромом намочите: и безо льда никогда плесени не будет."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "a8962838-cd81-4670-aaff-4d19bafcb22b",
                                "sense_id": "f57c91dc-c6c8-3a5c-b72f-17967408352c",
                                "text": "…Мужской тип, перейдя, так сказать, самого себя в Антиное и Гермафродите, двоится: с одной стороны, плотское и нравственное падение, загрязненные черты развратом и обжорством, кровью и всем на свете, безо лба, мелкие, как у гетеры Гелиогабала, или с опущенными щеками, как у Галбы; последний тип чудесно воспроизвелся в неаполитанском короле."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "f4f2baf7-4958-48fe-ba4c-cfb0ec8b01d5",
                                "sense_id": "f57c91dc-c6c8-3a5c-b72f-17967408352c",
                                "text": "А вот ночью, когда всякий остаётся ничем не скрыт, жутко безо сна лежать!"
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "62fa3b79-7456-4acf-ac4a-f7000f03fe53",
                        "source_entry_id": "f6b8a515-4182-35c0-ba38-f367b527597f",
                        "source_sense_id": "f57c91dc-c6c8-3a5c-b72f-17967408352c",
                        "target_lang_word": "without",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "without",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "d11fba57-5102-3c29-9f9f-11c8ba31e7e7",
                                        "entry_id": "f55e4992-3d87-3e81-9e00-23924a267fe3",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Outside, externally."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "archaic",
                                            "literary",
                                            "not-comparable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ebc73fb1-0a6c-4d58-8d36-f888476be4d7",
                                                "sense_id": "d11fba57-5102-3c29-9f9f-11c8ba31e7e7",
                                                "text": "And as each and all of them were warmed without by the sun, so each had a private little sun for her soul to bask in; some dream, some affection, some hobby, at least some remote and distant hope which, though perhaps starving to nothing, still lived on, as hopes will."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "9e4d0d66-ddc4-40a2-9dda-cc8f2bbe0e2e",
                                                "sense_id": "d11fba57-5102-3c29-9f9f-11c8ba31e7e7",
                                                "text": "Strange silence here: without, the sounding street\nHeralds the world's swift passage to the fire"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "8c736195-3b38-46e3-9200-726b6b104a33",
                                                "sense_id": "d11fba57-5102-3c29-9f9f-11c8ba31e7e7",
                                                "text": "I knew that someone had entered the house cautiously from without."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "eb7232e9-09e4-4aa3-aa7f-335c575eeb66",
                                                "sense_id": "d11fba57-5102-3c29-9f9f-11c8ba31e7e7",
                                                "text": "The feeling seemed to come not from without, but from within each body, as though every person had become a vibrating string."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a9d83ed8-9d8d-4b2d-b2ec-d013b9b8078f",
                                                "sense_id": "d11fba57-5102-3c29-9f9f-11c8ba31e7e7",
                                                "text": "Brainiac: This earthquake is quite literally worldwide.\nAlex Danvers: But the seismic activity [isn't] coming from within the planet, it's coming from without."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "5146a919-ce4d-3541-a51a-b7500c69478b",
                                        "entry_id": "f55e4992-3d87-3e81-9e00-23924a267fe3",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Lacking something; failing."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "not-comparable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "40957e11-8249-4112-8a65-35c7b0504faf",
                                                "sense_id": "5146a919-ce4d-3541-a51a-b7500c69478b",
                                                "text": "Being from a large, poor family, he learned to live without."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "42f821dd-f14a-4826-a57c-d95373b65adf",
                                                "sense_id": "5146a919-ce4d-3541-a51a-b7500c69478b",
                                                "text": "We've run out of bread; you'll have to do without until I can get to the bakeshop."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ab6a1c8e-a64f-426f-a09f-5f302df63679",
                                                "sense_id": "5146a919-ce4d-3541-a51a-b7500c69478b",
                                                "text": "Whose can be used with a following noun or without."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "c5025b0b-581d-4e8c-a4c2-bf27e8c1fbac",
                                                "sense_id": "5146a919-ce4d-3541-a51a-b7500c69478b",
                                                "text": "Communication is a kind of beauty, he said – and “beauty manifests itself from the noun itself, without strawberries on the cake.”"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "297096a1-5805-3951-b33f-f411038440b3",
                                        "entry_id": "f55e4992-3d87-3e81-9e00-23924a267fe3",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Without a condom being worn."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "euphemistic",
                                            "not-comparable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "53c7939a-895e-42ab-8067-76912a7faf20",
                                                "sense_id": "297096a1-5805-3951-b33f-f411038440b3",
                                                "text": "“What's within reason?” “Hand-job, blow-job, full sex — straight, full service. Greek, maybe, if you're not too big. Golden shower, if you like, but not reverse. No hardsports. And absolutely nothing without.”"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "without",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "6d3be5a1-4d20-3349-99bd-7b7def8e9e41",
                                        "entry_id": "ff7bccb1-95b3-3e6a-945b-dd1d7ebbe3de",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Outside of, beyond."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "archaic",
                                            "literary"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "3c3aee47-226b-48af-a278-23ee4057adf0",
                                                "sense_id": "6d3be5a1-4d20-3349-99bd-7b7def8e9e41",
                                                "text": "MACBETH: There's blood upon your face.\nFIRST MURDERER: 'Tis Banquo's then.\nMACBETH: 'Tis better thee without than he within."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "18cbb198-21e8-4ad4-8960-6b6a39bc945f",
                                                "sense_id": "6d3be5a1-4d20-3349-99bd-7b7def8e9e41",
                                                "text": "Without the gate / Some drive the cars, and some the coursers rein."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "76b4a788-92a4-4fb9-82a6-0df47508270e",
                                                "sense_id": "6d3be5a1-4d20-3349-99bd-7b7def8e9e41",
                                                "text": "From thence we came without the Eaſtern gate, (ſtanding on a low Banke, called the daughter of Syon, that over-toppeth the valley of Iehoſaphat,) unto an immoveable ſtone, upon the which they ſaid St. Stephen was ſtoned to death, the firſt Martyr of the Chriſtian faith; and the faithfull fore-runner of many noble followers."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "6256ba69-c685-4a32-ad25-ebfb39b6fc31",
                                                "sense_id": "6d3be5a1-4d20-3349-99bd-7b7def8e9e41",
                                                "text": "Eternity, before the world and after, is without our reach."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "2139b83e-5707-4c3a-9a25-118ba86b2d9c",
                                                "sense_id": "6d3be5a1-4d20-3349-99bd-7b7def8e9e41",
                                                "text": "[…] though it was pitch-dark, and we were obliged to be escorted by grooms and groomlings with candles and lanterns; a very necessary precaution, as the winds blew not more violently without the house than within."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "d9579106-94a8-4cad-a75d-bfb713eaa5a5",
                                                "sense_id": "6d3be5a1-4d20-3349-99bd-7b7def8e9e41",
                                                "text": "[...] nor shall any slave holder be allowed to emancipate his or her slave or slaves without the consent of congress, unless he or she shall send his or her slave or slaves without the limits of the republic [of Texas]."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "275111f6-fddd-3811-aa1e-bda3e5a39e23",
                                        "entry_id": "ff7bccb1-95b3-3e6a-945b-dd1d7ebbe3de",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Not having, containing, characteristic of, etc."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "49d83480-617f-4c87-b8d4-4ed189e0e203",
                                                "sense_id": "275111f6-fddd-3811-aa1e-bda3e5a39e23",
                                                "text": "It was a mistake to leave my house without a coat."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "0696209b-f37b-4b92-80c6-631a893c70c7",
                                                "sense_id": "275111f6-fddd-3811-aa1e-bda3e5a39e23",
                                                "text": "I was without formal education but was well read and articulate."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "bd14b53b-9861-4b53-bfc2-98efed81dbca",
                                                "sense_id": "275111f6-fddd-3811-aa1e-bda3e5a39e23",
                                                "text": "From another point of view, it was a place without a soul. The well-to-do had hearts of stone; the rich were brutally bumptious; the Press, the Municipality, all the public men, were ridiculously, vaingloriously self-satisfied."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b8c0ecf6-877c-4cd7-aa7a-391620ca833f",
                                                "sense_id": "275111f6-fddd-3811-aa1e-bda3e5a39e23",
                                                "text": "One day my dreams were surely dying, dying, dying baby\nJust like a flower without rain"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "727b5597-26bb-4437-a081-c812c082ccf0",
                                                "sense_id": "275111f6-fddd-3811-aa1e-bda3e5a39e23",
                                                "text": "1967, Paul McCartney (writer), The Beatles, Sgt. Pepper's Lonely Hearts Club Band\nLife goes on within you and without you."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "0e04d497-ad0d-4c17-b6a1-6a7e55ad4b73",
                                                "sense_id": "275111f6-fddd-3811-aa1e-bda3e5a39e23",
                                                "text": "Even without hovering drones, a lurking assassin, a thumping score and a denouement, the real-life story of Edward Snowden, a rogue spy on the run, could be straight out of the cinema."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b84afd33-fbba-43f1-8694-62e68feca5f5",
                                                "sense_id": "275111f6-fddd-3811-aa1e-bda3e5a39e23",
                                                "text": "\"Read lips: Without gas or without you? Without you. Without light or without you? Without you. Without water or without you? Without you. Without food or without you? Without you.\n\"Cold, hunger, darkness and thirst are not as terrible and deadly for us as your \"friendship and brotherhood.\""
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "000c11db-2741-3093-924b-35d4e085d5cb",
                                        "entry_id": "ff7bccb1-95b3-3e6a-945b-dd1d7ebbe3de",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Not doing or not having done something."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a242f056-6e36-4180-923f-1f4da8a2e3fc",
                                                "sense_id": "000c11db-2741-3093-924b-35d4e085d5cb",
                                                "text": "He likes to eat everything without sharing."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "0b9074a2-469a-444f-b883-451a55e46546",
                                                "sense_id": "000c11db-2741-3093-924b-35d4e085d5cb",
                                                "text": "He shot without warning anyone."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "cdfaa06e-c620-40ad-8a88-2a75ea1d9ed6",
                                                "sense_id": "000c11db-2741-3093-924b-35d4e085d5cb",
                                                "text": "Without noticing it I grew old."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "4e99d3fd-4371-4fac-a451-899a008bc3c5",
                                                "sense_id": "000c11db-2741-3093-924b-35d4e085d5cb",
                                                "text": "But in the meantime Robin Hood and his band lived quietly in Sherwood Forest, without showing their faces abroad, for Robin knew that it would not be wise for him to be seen in the neighborhood of Nottingham, those in authority being very wroth with him."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "c7b30934-531e-4f05-a8eb-7d19a4af5e3d",
                                                "sense_id": "000c11db-2741-3093-924b-35d4e085d5cb",
                                                "text": "Athelstan Arundel walked home[…], foaming and raging. […] He walked the whole way, walking through crowds, and under the noses of dray-horses, carriage-horses, and cart-horses, without taking the least notice of them."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "without",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "eb5c34ef-9428-3dd8-ac59-200aecd83ac7",
                                        "entry_id": "a0bf050a-1a1f-347f-b309-1d19ded6ce7b",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Unless, except (introducing a clause)."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "archaic",
                                            "dialectal"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "8866cb08-8a45-4770-ac85-1bb4ed82346c",
                                                "sense_id": "eb5c34ef-9428-3dd8-ac59-200aecd83ac7",
                                                "text": "You don't know about me, without you have read a book by the name of \"The Adventures of Tom Sawyer,\" but that ain't no matter."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "90507b48-aedc-48a5-8b0b-0aa877858a75",
                                                "sense_id": "eb5c34ef-9428-3dd8-ac59-200aecd83ac7",
                                                "text": "‘Why,’ he blurted, ‘because they say I've no right to come up like this—without we mean to marry—’"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
